 Given that the surface area \(A\) of a sphere is \(196\pi\) square inches, we can use the formula for the surface area of a sphere, which is \(A = 4\pi r^2\). We can solve for the radius \(r\) of the sphere: \[
4\pi r^2 = 196\pi \implies r^2 = 49 \implies r = 7 \text{ inches}
\] The circumference \(C\) of a great circle of the sphere (which is the same as the circumference of a circle with radius \(r\)) is given by \(C = 2\pi r\). Substituting \(r = 7\) into the formula, we get \[
C = 2\pi \cdot 7 = 14\pi \text{ inches}
\] The number of inches in the circumference of a great circle of this sphere is \(14\pi\). </think> <answer> \(14\pi\) </answer>

